  "id": "individual-psychology",
  "term": "individual psychology",
  "definition": "Individual psychology is the branch of psychology that studies how one psychological individual differs from others. It focuses on variations among people, such as differences in temperament, mental type, sex-related mental differences, genius, mental defect, criminality, and traits associated with social groups or professions.",
